{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026022400383660895daa7d84431c","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can see the structure now. The `trinity-nexus/core/src/root.zig` is a simpler module root. The current `src/trinity.zig` is more comprehensive.\n\nLooking at the task requirements and the current state:\n\n1. The files in `trinity-nexus/` are already duplicates of files in `src/`\n2. The build.zig references `src/` files, not `trinity-nexus/` files\n3. The migration should update the build file to use the trinity-nexus modules\n\nBut there's a nuance - looking at build.zig line 18-22:\n```zig\n// VIBEEC compiler module — single source of truth from trinity-nexus/lang\nconst trinity_lang_mod = b.createModule(.{\n    .root_source_file = b.path(\"trinity-nexus/lang/src/root.zig\"),\n    ...\n});\n```\n\nAnd the vibeec tests use this:\n```zig\n.imports = &.{\n    .{ .name = \"trinity-lang\", .module = trinity_lang_mod },\n},\n```\n\nBut for VSA, VM, etc., the build.zig still points to `src/vsa.zig`, `src/vm.zig` instead of using the trinity-nexus/core module.\n\nThe migration strategy should be:\n1. Create trinity-nexus modules for core, lang, symb in build.zig\n2. Update references to use these modules\n3. Remove duplicate files from src/ after confirming everything works\n\nLet me first check if there are files in `trinity-nexus/core/src/` that don't exist in `src/` or vice versa:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"981639af-0629-4dff-be1c-24fc61edb06a","uuid":"c00c7775-8c3a-4a0f-a0d9-21de8e52f210"}
